The runtime wheel contains Drawbridge Python source and project notices.
Its dependencies install separately and retain their own grants.
Conric 0.1.0 is a separately installed MIT configuration dependency; source: https://github.com/wolfmcnally/conric at ed9286297e92b8c049f70eb15a3b5556ed107ff0 (flat repository root).
Vellric is independently installed under AGPL-3.0-only.

The source archive includes public PDF test fixtures, separately licensed:
- RFC 8785: IETF Trust Legal Provisions; its complete copyright/legal notice
  remains inside tests/fixtures/rfc8785.pdf. Original source:
  https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8785.pdf
- OCRmyPDF test resources: CC-BY-SA-4.0, James R. Barlow, with source images
  attributed to Wikimedia by the upstream fixture provenance. Original
  sources and exact hashes remain in tests/fixtures/MANIFEST.md.
  Full license: LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt, from SPDX license-list-data;
  canonical legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
The fixtures are retained unmodified. MIT does not replace their grants.

Release builds use build-constraints.txt and the source uv.lock.

Native PowerPoint ingestion separately installs python-pptx 1.0.2 (MIT),
lxml 6.1.3 (BSD-3-Clause and independent native/component notices), and
XlsxWriter 3.3.1 (BSD-2-Clause). These binaries are not vendored in the
Drawbridge wheel or source archive. The selected lxml wheel lists iconv
under LGPL 2.1; redistribution of dependency binaries retains its applicable
obligations. Exact dependency notices are cataloged in references/README.md.
First-party presentation tests synthesize their own decks; downloaded
qualification decks and derivatives are not distributed.
